Title: COLD HANDOFF
Author: Daniel Crowe
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:

INT. COUNTY RECORDS OFFICE - DAY

AMIRA FAROOQ, 30s, meticulous, pulls a property file. A SILVER KEY sits on
her desk tag from a prior case.

AMIRA
Parcel 4421 — leased to Kline Logistics, sublet through Ruiz Holdings.

INT. DETECTIVE BUREAU - DAY

DETECTIVE ROSS briefs the squad. DETECTIVE VANCE stands by the map wall.

DETECTIVE ROSS
Harbor unit is active again. Farooq's records put Elena Ruiz on the lease.

DETECTIVE VANCE
And Marcus Kline on the tenant side. We watch before we move.

INT. ELENA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Rain on the glass. ELENA packs a small bag. MARCUS checks the locks.

ELENA
My sister cannot hear about this. Promise me.

MARCUS
She won't. Not from me.

INT. HARBOR WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Forklift beeps in the distance. MARCUS and JORDAN inventory crates.

MARCUS
The ledger stays in the office safe until we move.

JORDAN
Then we move fast. Ross is circling.

INT. ALL-NIGHT DINER - NIGHT

AMIRA meets THEO, nervous informant, in a back booth.

THEO
Vance's team pulled footage from the cafe. They know about the warehouse.

AMIRA
Give me a name I can verify.

Theo writes on a napkin and slides it under the salt shaker.

INT. WAREHOUSE OFFICE - NIGHT

MARCUS opens the safe. The BLUE LEDGER is inside, intact.

He photographs three pages, returns the ledger, and resets the combination dial.

INT. POLICE EVIDENCE ROOM - DAY

ROSS catalogs items from a prior raid. VANCE pins a still of MARCUS leaving the cafe.

DETECTIVE VANCE
Farooq can tie the lease to Ruiz by Friday.

DETECTIVE ROSS
Then we bring Elena in again. Voluntary first.

INT. PARKING GARAGE - NIGHT

JORDAN revs the engine. MARCUS sets the RED BRIEFCASE in the back seat.

JORDAN
If Ross has the warehouse, we are walking into a box.

MARCUS
We go tonight or we lose the window.

INT. AMIRA'S OFFICE - NIGHT

Amira cross-references the napkin address with county maps. Her phone buzzes —
a text from Ross: Can you sit in on the Ruiz interview tomorrow?

She types: On my way in early.

INT. POLICE INTERVIEW ROOM - DAY

ROSS and AMIRA sit across from ELENA. Water untouched.

DETECTIVE ROSS
Walk us through the sublease. Start with Kline Logistics.

ELENA
I rent space. Tenants handle their own operations.

Amira watches Elena — calm, rehearsed, giving nothing extra.

FADE OUT.

THE END
